<%# The composer, which always states which encryption it is about to use.

    Modelled on Gossip's STRONG / BASIC ENCRYPTION indicator: the user should
    never have to infer whether a message leaks its metadata.

    Wrapped in its own Turbo Frame so the :checking state can resolve itself: the
    Stimulus controller reloads just this frame until the peer's kind 10050 has
    been looked up. Nothing else on the page moves.

    turbo-permanent because live thread updates arrive as page refreshes (see
    show.html.erb): morphing this frame would reset the textarea to the
    server-rendered empty state, wiping a half-typed reply the moment a message
    came in. Frame reloads (the :checking poll) are unaffected. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(conversation, :composer), data: { turbo_permanent: "" } do %>
  <%= render "conversations/composer_body", conversation: conversation, delivery: delivery %>
<% end %>
